course: dictionary
lesson: 2092
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. «Content» is one of these words. It can be a noun, an adjective, or part of a phrase.
explain: Listen to the stress. In CON-tent, the stress is on the first part, and the word is a noun meaning the things inside something. In con-TENT, the stress is on the second part, and the word is an adjective meaning happy and satisfied. «The contents of the box spilled out» is the first kind. «The cat lay content by the fire» is the second kind.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. If it is about a box, bag, bottle or page, content probably means what is inside it. If it is about a book, film or website, it probably means what it is about. If it is about a feeling, it means happy with what you have.
fact: Content (CON-tent, noun) means the things inside a box, bag or bottle.
fact: The content of a book, film or website is what it is about, its ideas and information.
fact: Content (con-TENT, adjective) means happy and satisfied with what you have.
fact: The contents page of a book lists its chapters.
fact: Phrases to know: table of contents, online content, sugar content, and content with something.
exercise: «The contents of the box were spilled all over the floor.» What does contents mean here? | The price of the box | *The things inside the box | The people who packed it | The colour of the box
exercise: «The cat lay content by the fire, purring softly.» What does content mean here? | *Happy and satisfied | Written in a neat list | Full of information | Very angry
exercise: «Some online content is not suitable for children, so report it.» What does content mean here? | A list of chapters at the front of a book | *Material such as pictures, videos and words online | A happy, calm feeling | The things inside a bottle
test: Which meaning fits «The age rating warned about the game's scary content»? | *What the game is about, such as its scenes and material | The things inside the game box | A page that lists the game's levels | Happy and satisfied with the game
test: «She was content with her small garden.» What does content mean? | A page listing its chapters | Material on a screen | *Happy and satisfied | The sugar in her garden
exam: «The sugar content of this biscuit is high.» What does content mean? | A page that lists the biscuit's chapters | Happy with the biscuit | *The amount of sugar inside it | Online material about biscuits
